    "lengthM": 78.0,
    "diameterM": 35.7,
    "surfaceEmissivePowerKwM2": 265.0,
    "note": "SEP is the midpoint of the 257-273 kW/m2 range Raj (2005) reports over the entire visible fire area. The radiative fraction is NOT reported for these tests; 0.25 sits inside the 0.12-0.32 span Raj's Table 1 shows across the LNG series. Since the model derives SEP as chi*Q/(pi*D*L), this check tests the flame-length correlation and that assumed fraction jointly. Flame length read off Figure 4 of Wang et al. (2014), which plots the measured value at D=35 m; not a tabulated number."
